              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are rendering the Ready for Offers widget from this authoritative data:\n\n{{$context.$variables.data}}\n\nOutput exactly one multiRecordWidget using the app standard format. Do not output markdown, raw JSON, explanations, or text outside the widget.\n\nWidget title: Let's get some candidates hired\nColumns, in this exact order: Requisition, Candidate Name, Feedback Summary, Average Rating.\n\nEligibility and ordering rules:\n- The data is already filtered to candidates whose next immediate phase is Offer and who have completed feedback.\n- Do not exclude candidates because TotalScore, AverageRating, or any score/rating is null, blank, or zero.\n- Show at most 5 rows in the order provided.\n- Positive candidates are already ordered before borderline candidates.\n- Do not display duplicate candidates.\n\nAction rules:\n- Use PrimaryActionText and PrimaryActionCommand exactly as provided for each row.\n- Positive candidates must show Move Forward.\n- Borderline candidates must show More Details and must never show Move Forward.\n\nDisplay rules:\n- Average Rating must show stars when AverageRating exists; otherwise show exactly \"Rating Not Provided\".\n- Do not display Total Score.\n- For each row, summarize why the candidate is positive or borderline in 20-25 words using only provided feedback, interview rounds, strengths, concerns, and consensus.\n- Do not mention filtering criteria to the user.\n- Do not fabricate data."
